    focus: null,
    question: "What is the difference between a stateful and stateless application?",
    slug: "stateful-vs-stateless",
    shortDescription: "Define and give examples.",
    sampleAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nStateless applications do not store any client-specific data between requests (e.g., REST API). Stateful applications maintain session state (e.g., user login). Stateless is easier to scale horizontally.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nThe interviewer is checking whether you can explain the boundary between the two choices in what is the difference between a stateful and stateless application and tie that difference to an engineering decision.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. Stateless applications do not store any client-specific data between requests (e.g., REST API).\n2. Stateful applications maintain session state (e.g., user login).\n3. Stateless is easier to scale horizontally.\n4. Connect the concept to latency, failure modes, capacity, consistency, and operational cost rather than discussing components in isolation..\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nExplain what problem each option solves, the trade-off between them, and when each is the better fit.\n\n**Example :**\nFor example, in a production application, choose the option whose behavior matches the requirement and compare the resulting operational consequence. Stateless applications do not store any client-specific data between requests (e.g., REST API).\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nIn a production application, engineers use this when they need the behavior described by the question. Stateless applications do not store any client-specific data between requests (e.g., REST API).\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Defining both sides but never stating the practical difference.\n- Choosing one option without naming the requirement that drives the choice.\n- Treating platform-specific behavior as a universal rule.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nState the decision rule early: when would you choose A, and when would you choose B? That is more useful than listing every secondary difference.",
