    sampleAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nPrometheus is a time-series database and monitoring system that scrapes metrics from targets. Grafana is a visualization tool that can query Prometheus (and other data sources) to create dashboards.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nThe interviewer is checking whether you can explain the boundary between the two choices in what is the difference between prometheus and grafana and tie that difference to an engineering decision.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. Prometheus is a time-series database and monitoring system that scrapes metrics from targets.\n2. Grafana is a visualization tool that can query Prometheus (and other data sources) to create dashboards.\n3. Connect the concept to latency, failure modes, capacity, consistency, and operational cost rather than discussing components in isolation..\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nExplain what problem each option solves, the trade-off between them, and when each is the better fit.\n\n**Example :**\nFor example, in a production application, choose the option whose behavior matches the requirement and compare the resulting operational consequence. Prometheus is a time-series database and monitoring system that scrapes metrics from targets.\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nIn a production application, engineers use this when they need the behavior described by the question. Prometheus is a time-series database and monitoring system that scrapes metrics from targets.\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Defining both sides but never stating the practical difference.\n- Choosing one option without naming the requirement that drives the choice.\n- Treating platform-specific behavior as a universal rule.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nState the decision rule early: when would you choose A, and when would you choose B? That is more useful than listing every secondary difference.",
